I don't think that the content of the potions or the vampires have to
turn to dust. It is not really canon in mythology. If they do depends
largely on the in-game/in-fiction explanation of vampirism.

In NetHack killing a vampire may leave a human corpse. Only Vlad's
body crumble into dust, normal vampires in NetHack don't.

In Slash'Em it's the same but there is the possibility of driving a
wooden stake through the heart of vampire. Then he does turn to dust.

